  "footnote": "Hands-on research experience (fieldwork, curation, laboratory work, or similar) is required with approval from both the advisor and DUS; waivers are rare and granted only in exceptional circumstances. This experience must be verified manually. Major courses require C or better. Select courses with the major advisor; coordinate intensive language training early when appropriate. No prerequisites are needed to declare. Optional honors requires a 3.5 major GPA, 3.0 overall GPA, a senior thesis, and ARKEO 4981 and ARKEO 4982; consult the DUS before the final year. Only ARKEO 4981 counts toward the major, within the 4-credit independent-study limit. Honors criteria apply starting with 2026-27 graduates.",
